course: biology
lesson: 81
title: The big cats house: lions and tigers up close
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: In the big cats house a lion may lie on a warm rock for your whole visit, and that is not laziness: a lion hunts in short, hard bursts, so it saves its strength by resting up to 20 hours a day.
explain: Then it gets up, roars, and the glass seems to shake; a roar can carry about 8 kilometres on a still night and tells other lions «this land is ours».
explain: Next door a tiger slides into its pool, because tigers come from hot, steamy forests and love water, and under its fur the skin itself is striped.
explain: Watch the lion lick its paw and you will see your own cat at home: same rough tongue, same washing, just two hundred times heavier.
explain: A big cat does not chase mice like Tom chases Jerry; a mouse is far too small to be worth the effort for a hunter that needs kilograms of meat a day.
fact: Lions sleep or rest for up to 20 hours a day, in the zoo and in the wild, and a house cat sleeps about 15.
fact: A lion's roar can be heard up to about 8 kilometres away; only the lion, tiger, leopard and jaguar can truly roar.
fact: In a wild pride the lionesses do most of the hunting, often together, while the maned male guards the land and the cubs.
fact: Tigers swim well and cool off in pools and rivers; most cats dislike water, but tigers, jaguars and fishing cats are happy swimmers.
fact: Walking the same line again and again is called pacing; it can mean a cat is bored, and good zoos change the enclosure and give puzzles to reduce it.
fact: A tiger's skin is striped under the fur, and no two tigers have the same stripes, so scientists tell them apart from camera photos.
fact: Deer see fewer colours than we do, so to them an orange tiger looks much like the green and brown leaves around it.
fact: White tigers are ordinary Bengal tigers with a rare gene; breeding close relatives to get them causes health problems, so good zoos no longer do it.
fact: Big cats are kept behind strong mesh, thick glass or a wide ditch called a moat, and keepers never go in with them.
fact: A lion's tongue is covered with tiny backward hooks that comb its fur and scrape meat off bones, like a house cat's but far rougher.
fact: A lion needs about 5 to 7 kilograms of meat a day, which would be hundreds of mice, so big cats hunt zebras, antelopes and other large animals.
exercise: How many hours a day can a lion sleep or rest? | Up to about 20 | About 6, like a busy adult | Only about 2, in short naps | It never sleeps in the day
exercise: Why does a lion rest so much? | It hunts in short, hard bursts and must save energy | It is bored stiff because it lives in a zoo and has nothing to do | Lions get ill if they move a lot | The sun makes all big cats sleepy
exercise: How far away can a lion's roar be heard on a still night? | Up to about 8 kilometres | About 80 metres | About 800 kilometres | Only inside its cage
exercise: Which group lists only cats that can truly roar? | Lion, tiger, leopard and jaguar | Lion, cheetah, puma and Eurasian lynx | Tiger, house cat, puma and cheetah | Lion, snow leopard, cheetah and puma
exercise: Who does most of the hunting in a wild lion pride? | The lionesses, often working together | The male with the biggest and darkest mane | The cubs, to practise | Each lion hunts only for itself
exercise: Why do tigers like to sit in water? | They come from hot forests and water cools them | They are hunting for the fish and sharks that hide in the pool | Water makes their stripes brighter | They cannot walk well on land
exercise: What is it called when a tiger walks the same line again and again? | Pacing | Stalking | Grooming | Migrating
exercise: Where are a tiger's stripes? | In the fur and in the skin underneath | Only on the tips of the hairs | Only on the fur, not the skin | Only on the tail and face
exercise: Why does an orange tiger hide well from deer? | Deer see fewer colours, so orange looks like the leaves | Deer are completely blind in the daytime and only see at night | Tigers turn green when they hunt | Deer only look up at the trees
exercise: What is a white tiger? | An ordinary Bengal tiger with a rare gene for pale fur | A separate kind of tiger from the snowy north | A tiger whose fur turned white with age | A cross between a tiger and a polar bear
exercise: What is a moat around a lion's enclosure? | A wide, deep ditch the lion cannot jump | A pool for the lion to drink from | A path for the keepers | A fence made of thin wire
exercise: Why does a lion lick its paw like a house cat? | Big cats wash themselves with their rough tongues too | It is tasting the paw for salt left by the sweat of the hunt | It is hurt and the zoo did not notice | Lions copy what they see visitors do
exercise: What makes a lion's tongue so rough? | Tiny backward hooks that comb fur and scrape bones | Sand stuck to it from the enclosure floor | Rows of small sharp teeth growing on the top of the tongue | Dry skin from too much sun
exercise: Why don't lions hunt mice? | A mouse is far too small to be worth the effort | Lions are terribly afraid of mice, like elephants in cartoons | Mice are too fast for any cat | Lions cannot see small things at all
exercise: About how much meat does a lion need each day? | About 5 to 7 kilograms | About 50 grams | About one mouse | About 500 kilograms
exercise: Why do good zoos no longer breed white tigers on purpose? | Breeding close relatives gives cubs health problems | White tigers are far too dangerous to keep near visitors | Visitors find white tigers boring | White tigers cannot eat meat
test: 3 lions on the rock and 2 tigers in the pool. how many legs is that | 20 | 12 | 16 | 24
test: In Tom and Jerry a cat chases a mouse every day. «so a lion would chase Jerry too right?» | No, a lion hunts big prey, a mouse is not worth it | Yes, every cat chases mice all day, big or small | Yes, lions mostly eat mice in the wild | No, lions are scared of mice
test: «that lion's useless, hasn't moved in an hour, is it ill or what» What is right? | Resting up to 20 hours a day is normal for a lion | It must be ill, because healthy lions never stop moving around | It is stuffed and not a real lion | Zoo lions are given sleeping pills
test: Count the ears: 4 lions and 1 tiger are lying in the sun. How many ears altogether? | 10 | 5 | 8 | 20
test: A friend says the male lion with the big mane is the best hunter of the pride. What would you say? | The lionesses do most of the hunting; he guards the land | Right, only males hunt in a pride while the females mind the cubs | Right, the mane helps him hide in the grass | The cubs do all the hunting
test: What would happen if a keeper shaved a patch of a tiger's fur? | The stripes would still show on the skin | The skin would be plain pink underneath | The fur would grow back with no stripes | The tiger would lose all its stripes
test: «how can a bright orange tiger hide, it sticks out a mile» What is right? | To deer, orange looks like the green and brown leaves | Tigers only hunt at night, so their colour does not matter at all | Deer can smell but not see at all | Tigers are really green in the wild
test: A cartoon cat is always sitting in the bath, hating every second. Which big cat would actually enjoy the bath? | A tiger | A cheetah | A snow leopard | A wild lynx
test: A pet shop says its white tiger cub is «a rare kind from the Arctic». What is true? | It is an ordinary Bengal tiger with a rare pale gene | Yes, white tigers live wild in the Arctic and hunt seals on the ice | It is a polar bear cub in disguise | It is a separate species found only in zoos
test: Why would a keeper hide meat in different places each day instead of always in one bowl? | It gives the cat something to search for and cuts down pacing | It makes the meat taste better and fresher after a day in the grass | So the visitors cannot see the food | So the lion eats less meat
test: 2 lions and 3 tigers. how many tails, and no it's not 20 lol | 5 | 20 | 10 | 4
exam: Identify the principal reason for which the lion rests for the greater part of each day. | It hunts in brief, strenuous bursts and must conserve energy | It is afflicted by grave illness whenever it is kept in captivity | It is nocturnal and incapable of any activity during the hours of daylight | It lacks entirely the muscles required for sustained movement
exam: Select the response consistent with the established facts concerning the white tiger. | It is a Bengal tiger bearing a rare gene that renders the fur pale | It constitutes a distinct species native to Arctic regions | It is the offspring of a tiger and a snow leopard | It is a tiger whose coat has faded with advanced age
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the division of labour within a wild lion pride? | The lionesses conduct most hunting; the male defends the territory | The male conducts all hunting whilst the lionesses remain with the cubs | Each member hunts exclusively for itself | Hunting is undertaken solely by the cubs
exam: It is given that a lion requires between five and seven kilograms of meat daily. Determine the most accurate explanation of why it does not pursue mice. | A mouse yields far too little food to repay the chase | Lions are incapable of perceiving animals of so small a size | Mice are toxic to all members of the cat family | Lions are known to be afraid of mice
